{
  "_about": "The label rule (labels-and-surfaces.md § What a label says) as conformance vectors: a label document, the renderer's clock and the outcome every renderer must reach, wherever it runs. caption: draw the label text. card: a quiet card with wall_name. blank: draw nothing. The rule, in full: showing_art captions when label is present and is the card when it is null; in_use, dark and no_screen are blank; unassigned is the card; silent and unreachable caption while label is present and now is less than hold_seconds after since, and are blank otherwise, including when since is null; a state the reader does not know is read as unreachable. A since later than now is a held state just entered, so it captions. Every document validates against schemas/label.v1.schema.json except those marked schema_valid false, whose one fault is a state from a later minor.",
  "hold_seconds": 1800,
